# Upstream's ignore rules, preserved verbatim.
#
# liberfa/erfa `.gitignore` at the pinned commit
# 1a8044cde5b7763295d472a6443387239127c6c8, all 24 patterns in their original
# order. None was removed, reordered relative to another, or weakened. These
# are autotools artefacts this fork never produces -- it compiles the library
# with Zig and never runs `bootstrap.sh`, `configure` or `make` -- and they are
# kept because upstream's own tree depends on them, not because this build
# needs them.
/aclocal.m4
/autom4te.cache/
/config.*
/configure
/depcomp
/erfa.pc
/install-sh
/libtool
/ltmain.sh
/m4/
/missing
/stamp-h?
/test-driver
.deps/
.dirstamp
.libs/
*.l[ao]
*.o
*~
Makefile
Makefile.in
/build-aux
src/t_erfa_c
erfa-*.tar.gz

# Re-inclusion: upstream's `/m4/` above is broad enough to swallow
# `m4/erfa-numver.m4`, which is upstream *source*, not a build artefact. That
# file records the rule that splits `PACKAGE_VERSION` into the three numeric
# macros this package's generated `config.h` carries
# (m4/erfa-numver.m4:22-24, matching configure.ac:5 and meson.build:3), it is
# listed in build.zig.zon's `.paths`, and its SHA-256 is a record in
# UPSTREAM.sha256. Dropping the pattern would delete a file the integrity gate
# checks; keeping the pattern without this exception would stop that file from
# being tracked at all. Both the rule and the file stand.
!/m4/
!/m4/erfa-numver.m4

# This fork's own build outputs.
#
# `/config.*` above already covers a root `config.h`, but this build never
# writes one into the source tree: `config.h` is generated into the Zig build
# cache by `addWriteFiles` and put on the include path from there, so there is
# nothing in this directory for that rule to catch. `.zig-cache/`,
# `zig-out/` and `zig-pkg/` are this fork's outputs and are excluded from
# `.paths` in build.zig.zon for the same reason.
/.zig-cache/
/zig-out/
/zig-pkg/
# The consumer package is a separate Zig package with its own build root, so
# it has its own three. Anchored at `consumer/` because these names are
# unanchored elsewhere in this file's upstream half only where upstream needed
# them to be.
/consumer/.zig-cache/
/consumer/zig-out/
/consumer/zig-pkg/

# Nothing else is ignored. In particular the fork's own sources and records --
# `zig/`, `build.zig`, `build.zig.zon`, `cross-test.profile.sh`, `tests.zig`,
# `smoke.zig`, `consumer/src/`, `UPSTREAM.md`, `UPSTREAM.sha256`, `NOTICE.md`,
# `README.zig.md`, `FORK-NOTES.md`, `CHANGELOG.md` and
# `.github/workflows/verify.yml` -- match no pattern above, and `make`, the
# autotools output name, matches no file in this tree.